Describing takes RIGHT_W, as changing an object does,
so a capability with fewer rights cannot describe itself;
a describing call succeeds on any filled slot whatever its rights.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a describing call failed on a filled slot

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -994,7 +994,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
         return err;
     }
     /* Describing grants no authority, so every type takes it, with no right, before the types' own checks. */
-    if (op == OP_CAP_INFO) {
+    if (op == OP_CAP_INFO && (cap.rights & RIGHT_W)) {
         return cap_info(&cap, arg);
     }
 
